content.p:
the 1980 Act means the Local Government, Planning and Land Act 1980

1980 c. 65.
								;

the 1990 Act means the Town and Country Planning Act 1990

1990 c. 8.
								;

certification date means the date on which the certified non-domestic rating income for the relevant year is certified under regulation 9 of the Rates Retention Regulations

S.I. 2013/452; relevant amending instruments are S.I. 2015/628, 2016/1268, 2017/1321, 2020/449, 2021/262, 404, 2022/784.
								;

the Corporation means the body corporate known as the Hartlepool Development Corporation established by article 3 of the Hartlepool Development Corporation (Establishment) Order 2023

S.I. 2023/104.
								;

the Hazardous Substances Act means the Planning (Hazardous Substances) Act 1990

1990 c. 10.
								;

the Listed Buildings Act means the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990

1990 c. 9.
								;

preceding year means the financial year

See section 145(3) of the Local Government Finance Act 1988 for the meaning of “financial year”.
								 immediately preceding the relevant year;

Rates Retention Regulations means the Non-Domestic Rating (Rates Retention) Regulations 2013

S.I. 2013/452.
								;

section 151 officer means the person who is for the time being appointed by the previous authority to be responsible for the administration of its financial affairs

See section 151 of the Local Government Act 1972 (c. 70).
								;

A is the percentage that is the previous authority’s local share for the relevant year as determined in accordance with paragraph 4 of Schedule 7B to the 1988 Act

Schedule 7B was inserted by Schedule 1 to the Local Government Finance Act 2012 (c. 17).
									;

In this article, the “consolidated gross assets” of a person is a reference to the gross assets of that person together with any subsidiary (within the meaning of section 1159 of the Companies Act 2006

2006 c. 46.
								).

in the case of a stop notice, until the notice ceases to have effect (construed in accordance with section 184(4) or 184(5) of the 1990 Act

Section 184(4) and (5) was amended by paragraph 28 of Schedule 7 to the Planning and Compensation Act 1991.
											);

area application means an application for the designation of a neighbourhood development area made under section 61G of the 1990 Act

Section 61G was inserted by paragraph 2 of Part 1 of Schedule 9 to the 2011 Act and amended by section 5(3) of the Neighbourhood Planning Act 2017 (c. 20) and section 139 of the Housing and Planning Act 2016.
											;

neighbourhood forum application means an application for designation of a neighbourhood forum made by an organisation or body under section 61F of the 1990 Act

Section 61F was inserted by paragraph 2 of Part 1 of Schedule 9 to the Localism Act 2011, and amended by section 5(2) of the Neighbourhood Planning Act 2017.
											;
